@startuml authorization-eidas-sequence
skinparam svgDimensionStyle false

participant App
participant "FHIR Server\n(EU Authorization Resource Server)" as FHIR
participant "EU Authorization Server" as AS
participant "Authentication Service" as AuthN
participant "eIDAS / EUDI Wallet" as eIDAS

note over AS, AuthN
    Distinct logical roles; MAY be grouped in one implementation.
    Separate-service authentication interface is deployment-defined.
    AS / FHIR co-location is a separate optional choice.
    No universal or central EU server is implied.
end note

== Get Access Token ==

alt Pre-authorized Backend Service
    App -> AS++: Token request\nclient_credentials + asymmetric client authentication
    App <-- AS--: Access token
    note over AS, AuthN: No runtime end-user authentication in Backend Services
else Interactive user or patient launch
    App -> AS++: Authorization request\n(selected SMART or IUA flow)
    AS -> AuthN++: Arrange user authentication\n(deployment-defined integration)
    opt Wallet selected as authentication means
        AuthN -> eIDAS++: Request user-approved presentation
        AuthN <-- eIDAS--: Presentation, not an API access token
    end
    note right of AuthN: Authenticate user; validate evidence\nor trusted upstream result
    AS <-- AuthN--: Trusted authentication result\n(format and interface deployment-defined)
    note right of AS
        Validate result
        Establish user session
        Apply authorization policy
    end note
    App <-- AS--: Redirect with authorization code
    App -> AS++: Token request\n(code + PKCE for SMART; client auth as applicable)
    App <-- AS--: Access token and applicable launch context
end

== Access Content ==

App -> FHIR++: Protected resource request (access token)
note right of FHIR: Validate / introspect token\nEnforce granted scopes and local policy
App <-- FHIR--: Authorized response

@enduml